# Design System UI Conventions

Wave D + Wave E established a single, role-first design system at
`services/design-system/` (npm workspace `@leo/design-system`). All new
UI MUST consume that system. Direct `@mui/material` imports inside
`services/ui/src/app/admin/knowledge/**` are a regression and will be
blocked by ESLint in Phase 7.

## 1. Source of truth

- **Workspace package:** `@leo/design-system`. Imported as
  `import { StatHero, ToolbarActions, ... } from "@leo/design-system";`.
- **Index:** `services/design-system/src/index.ts` re-exports
  `tokens`, `motion`, `fonts`, `roles`, `copy`, `primitives`.
- **Primitives:** live in `services/design-system/src/primitives/`.
  At time of writing: `KnowledgePageLayout`, `IntroCard`, `StatHero`,
  `MetricTile`, `ProgressStrip`, `SegmentedTabs`, `FilterBar`,
  `ToolbarActions`, `ReviewListCard`, `DataGridCard`, `TaskQueue`,
  `ProgressiveReveal`. Do not duplicate any of these in `services/ui`.

## 2. Pick the right primitive

| Surface                                | Primitive(s)                                 |
| -------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Page chrome (intro + tabs)             | `KnowledgePageLayout` + `IntroCard`          |
| Top-of-page stats                      | `StatHero` (4 tiles), or `MetricTile` grid   |
| Page-level primary action              | `ToolbarActions` (single `variant: "primary"`) |
| Status / category filter               | `SegmentedTabs` (with `tabs` / `value` / `aria-label`) |
| Free-text search + facet chips         | `FilterBar`                                  |
| Long row of editable items             | `ReviewListCard`                             |
| Tabular data with sort / select        | `DataGridCard`                               |
| Inline progressive disclosure          | `ProgressiveReveal`                          |
| Multi-step workflow card               | Local `StepCard` pattern (see Clinical Guidelines) |
| Multi-stage progress                   | `ProgressStrip`                              |

If the surface needs something the primitives do not yet cover, raise
a new primitive in `@leo/design-system` rather than re-implementing it
inside `services/ui/src`.

## 3. Tokens, never magic numbers

- **Spacing:** 8pt grid via `tokens/spacing` (`xxs:4 / xs:8 / sm:12 /
  md:16 / lg:24 / xl:32 / xxl:48`). Values in `sx` should map to these.
- **Radius:** `tokens/spacing.radius` (`xs:4 / sm:8 / md:12 / lg:16 /
  pill:999`). Cards default to `md` (12).
- **Elevation:** `tokens/spacing.elevation.card / .popover / .modal`.
- **Motion:** `tokens/motion` (`default` 180ms easeOut, `route` spring,
  `hover` 120ms easeOut, `instant`). Always wrap with `useMotion()` so
  reduced-motion users collapse to 0ms automatically.
- **Roles:** `roles` exports the role-first IA (Clinical Lead, QA / RA
  Lead, Solutions Architect, Operator). Use `useRole()` to gate
  features, never hardcode role strings.

## 4. Canonical card pattern

The card pattern shipped through Wave E (DomainCard, PackageCard,
PathwayCard, StepCard, ReviewListCard) is the visual baseline. New
cards MUST match it:

- `borderRadius: 12` (number) or `"12px"` (string) -- both accepted.
- `padding: 18` or `p: "18px"`.
- `border: "1px solid #E2E8F0"` (or `borderColor: "divider"`).
- 3px-wide left accent strip, tone-coded by status:
  ```tsx
  <span
    aria-hidden="true"
    style={{
      position: "absolute",
      left: 0,
      top: 14,
      bottom: 14,
      width: 3,
      borderRadius: 2,
      background: accent,
    }}
  />
  ```
- `minHeight: 168` for grid cards (so the grid stays tidy on the wide
  layout).
- Stagger entry via framer-motion `delay = Math.min(index, 12) * 0.04`
  (see `PathwayCard.tsx`).

## 5. Knowledge tab width parity

`services/ui/src/app/admin/knowledge/page.tsx` owns the `TAB_WIDTH`
map. All eight Knowledge tabs render at `"wide"` (1600px). Reading-
oriented surfaces stay on `"reading"` (1280px). Do not split a tab
into a third width without raising a DI; users complained loudly when
widths drifted.

## 6. Adaptive density

Density is read from `useDensity()` (Phase 1 cont, in flight). Until
the context provider lands, primitives accept a `density?: "airy" |
"compact"` prop with `"airy"` as the default. New components MUST
accept density as a prop and respect it for vertical padding.

## 7. Framer Motion is the only animation library

- Import as `import { motion as fm } from "framer-motion";`.
- Use `fm.div`, `fm.section`, `fm.button`. Never animate via raw CSS
  transitions for new components.
- Stagger lists with `delay = Math.min(index, MAX) * STEP` (typical
  values: `MAX=12`, `STEP=0.04`).
- For a hover lift, prefer `whileHover={{ boxShadow: ... }}` over
  changing `y` so it stays accessible to keyboard-focus users.
- Always honour reduced-motion: when `useMotion()` returns
  `prefersReducedMotion`, fall through to `motion.instant` so the
  duration is 0ms.

## 8. MUI is allowed -- but as an internal renderer

Outside `@leo/design-system`, `@mui/material` is permitted only for
low-level renderers (`Box`, `Stack`, `Typography`, `Button`, `Chip`,
`Dialog`, `TextField`, `Tooltip`, `IconButton`, `Skeleton`, `Alert`).
Do not introduce a new MUI surface that the design system already
covers. If you find yourself rebuilding `Tabs`, `Card`, `CardContent`,
or `LinearProgress`-based stat tiles, use the design-system primitive
instead.

- Import from specific paths: `import Box from "@mui/material/Box";`
  (never barrel imports). This keeps Turbopack incremental builds fast.
- Never use raw `style={{ ... }}` on MUI components -- use `sx`. The
  one allowed exception is the framer-motion `style` prop on
  `motion.div` etc., where `sx` is not available.

## 9. Page structure checklist

Every Knowledge / Admin page should follow the same skeleton:

```tsx
import {
  StatHero,
  SegmentedTabs,
  ToolbarActions,
  type StatTile,
  type ToolbarAction,
} from "@leo/design-system";

export default function MyPage() {
  // ... data + state
  const stats: StatTile[] = useMemo(() => /* ... */, [data]);
  const toolbarActions: ToolbarAction[] = [
    {
      id: "primary-action",
      label: "Do the thing",
      icon: <AddIcon fontSize="small" />,
      variant: "primary",  // exactly one primary per page
      onClick: () => /* ... */,
    },
  ];

  return (
    <Box>
      <StatHero stats={stats} />
      {/* error alert */}
      <Box sx={{ display: "flex", justifyContent: "space-between", flexWrap: "wrap", gap: 2, mb: 2 }}>
        <SegmentedTabs tabs={...} value={...} onChange={...} aria-label="..." />
        <ToolbarActions actions={toolbarActions} />
      </Box>
      {/* loading / empty / no-match / data */}
    </Box>
  );
}
```

## 10. Copy + role-first tone

All UI text MUST go through `services/design-system/src/copy/` so the
role-first IA can reuse it. Patient- or non-specialist-facing copy
also follows `health-literacy.mdc` (reading age 9-11, plain English,
short sentences, active voice).

## 11. ASCII only

All source files (TSX, TS, comments, copy strings) MUST be ASCII --
no em-dashes, curly quotes, arrows, or box-drawing characters. See
`ascii-only.mdc`. PowerShell on Windows breaks otherwise.

## 12. File-size discipline

UI files follow the project-wide limits in `code-quality.mdc`:

- Target <=300 LOC, hard limit 500 LOC.
- When a page approaches 500 LOC, split it into sibling modules in the
  same directory: e.g. `pathways/{page.tsx, PathwayCard.tsx,
  dialogs.tsx, templates.ts, types.ts}`. The `page.tsx` keeps state +
  handlers; sibling modules are presentational.
- Dialog clusters live in a sibling `dialogs.tsx` (or
  `<Feature>Dialog/` folder for >2 sub-components).
